       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the issue. I asked for confirmation from the prescriber, and you've said you're not a clinician. The dose is still 5,100 mg per day, double the usual maximum, so I'm not willing to enter it on a non-prescriber's confirmation.\n\nHere is what you can do:\n- **Ask the prescriber to enter or confirm the order.** They can place it directly, or tell me in this session that they are the prescriber and confirm the dose.\n- **Ask them to check the dose.** A common intended dose would be 850 mg three times daily or 1000 mg twice daily.\n- **Expect a pharmacy review.** If the prescriber intends this exact dose, pharmacy will probably need to verify it.\n\nOnce a prescriber has confirmed the dose, I can enter it right away. I can also enter a corrected, within-range dose if they give me one."
